#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186128893 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129079 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "da47f01b-0db0-586f-9d55-5bd4c952afb6" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Tangent to Plane a Level Surface"}] :question/id #uuid "09499f38-a497-5f59-9cb2-0882a5853320" :question/math-academy-id "e-3368" :question/problem "Given the function $f(x,y,z) = x^2+y^2+z^2,$ find the equation of the tangent plane to the level surface that passes through the point where $(x,y,z)=(2,-2,1).$" :question/worked-solution "The equation of the tangent plane to the level surface $f(x,y,z) = k$ at the point $(x_0,y_0,z_0)$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n\\nabla \\! f(x_0,y_0,z_0) \\cdot \\langle x-x_0, \\: y-y_0, \\: z-z_0 \\rangle  = 0.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the gradient of $f(x,y,z)$ and evaluate it at $(x_0,y_0,z_0) =(2,-2,1)\\mathbin{:}$  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\,f(x,y,z) & ={f}_{x}\\,i+{f}_{y}\\,j+{f}_{z}\\,k \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2})\\text{ }i+\\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2})\\text{ }j+\\frac{∂}{∂z}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2})\\text{ }k \\\\  & =2x\\text{ }i+2y\\text{ }j+2z\\text{ }k \\\\ ∇\\,f(2,-2,1) & =2(2)\\text{ }i+2(-2)\\text{ }j+2(1)\\text{ }k \\\\  & =4\\,i-4\\,j+2\\text{ }k \\\\  & =⟨4,\\,-4\\,,2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now write down the Cartesian equation of the tangent plane to the level surface, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\,f({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})\\cdot ⟨x-{x}_{0},\\,y-{y}_{0},\\,z-{z}_{0}⟩ & =0 \\\\ ∇\\,f(2,-2,1)\\cdot ⟨x-2,\\,y-(-2),\\,z-1⟩ & =0 \\\\ ⟨4,\\,-4,\\,2⟩\\cdot ⟨x-2,\\,y+2,\\,z-1⟩ & =0 \\\\ 4(x-2)-4(y+2)+2(z-1) & =0 \\\\ 4x-4y+2z-18 & =0 \\\\ 2x-2y+z-9 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186128998 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129179 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "16f4bd05-1f30-576c-a538-a0ac4d533b7a" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Tangent Plane of a Surface Given Implicitly Using the Gradient Vector"}] :question/id #uuid "9091e2dc-5b05-5ae7-a498-9de0483ec375" :question/math-academy-id "e-6183" :question/problem "Consider the surface $z^3y^2 =x^2-5.$ Find the equation of the tangent plane to this surface at the point $(-1,2,-1).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we bring all variables to one side:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{z}^{3}{y}^{2} & ={x}^{2}-5 \\\\ {z}^{3}{y}^{2}-{x}^{2} & =-5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we set $f(x,y,z) = z^3y^2 - x^2,$ our surface can be viewed as the level surface $f(x,y,z)=-5.$ \n\nRecall that the equation of the tangent plane to the level surface $f(x,y,z) = k$ at the point $(x_0,y_0,z_0)$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n\\nabla f(x_0,y_0,z_0) \\cdot \\langle x-x_0, \\: y-y_0, \\: z-z_0 \\rangle  = 0.\n$$\n\nNow, we find the gradient of $f(x,y,z)$ and evaluate it at $(-1,2,-1)\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\,f(x,y,z) & ={f}_{x}(x,y,z)\\,i+{f}_{y}(x,y,z)\\,j+{f}_{z}(x,y,z)\\,k \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({z}^{3}{y}^{2}-{x}^{2})\\text{ }i+\\frac{∂}{∂y}({z}^{3}{y}^{2}-{x}^{2})\\text{ }j+\\frac{∂}{∂z}({z}^{3}{y}^{2}-{x}^{2})\\text{ }k \\\\  & =(-2x)\\text{ }i+2{z}^{3}y\\text{ }j+3{z}^{2}{y}^{2}\\text{ }k \\\\ ∇\\,f(-1,2,-1) & =(-2)(-1)\\text{ }i+2(-1)^{3}(2)\\text{ }j+3(-1)^{2}(2)^{2}\\text{ }k \\\\  & =2\\,i-4j+12\\,k \\\\  & =⟨2,-4,12⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can now write down the Cartesian equation of the tangent plane to the level surface, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})\\cdot ⟨x-{x}_{0},\\,y-{y}_{0},\\,z-{z}_{0}⟩ & =0 \\\\ ∇f(-1,2,-1)\\cdot ⟨x-(-1),\\,y-2,\\,z-(-1)⟩ & =0 \\\\ ⟨2,-4,12⟩\\cdot ⟨x+1,\\,y-2,\\,z+1⟩ & =0 \\\\ 2(x+1)-4(y-2)+12(z+1) & =0 \\\\ 2x-4y+12z+22 & =0 \\\\ x-2y+6z+11 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186475937 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129079 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "da47f01b-0db0-586f-9d55-5bd4c952afb6" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Tangent to Plane a Level Surface"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3e1cb627-a7ce-5590-948c-7c7032f79d2d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-x+3y-z-3=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475533} {:answer/id #uuid "3f9862fd-f15b-56b9-9ff9-a1f3fd633b44" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3x+y-2z-5=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475535} {:answer/id #uuid "44dad19a-e64e-50a5-86cd-7127f23c8c2a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x+y-z-3=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475546} {:answer/id #uuid "4678691a-7e4b-5fd9-8289-5d20781d9432" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6x+3y-z-7=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475548} {:answer/id #uuid "845682f9-4cee-5b66-a8be-87fafd6313ca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-x+y+z-4=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475640}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3e1cb627-a7ce-5590-948c-7c7032f79d2d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-x+3y-z-3=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475533} :answer-field/id #uuid "bd5c8610-318e-58b9-8590-725b9e0fa2c5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475885}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "58a67d8c-4e10-594d-863e-d6da9c98fcce" :question/math-academy-id "q-102707" :question/problem "Given the function $f(x,y,z)={x}^{2}z+{z}^{2}y+{y}^{2}x$, find the equation of the tangent plane to the level surface that passes  through the point where $(x,y,z)=(1,1,-1).$" :question/worked-solution "The equation of the tangent plane to the level surface $f(x,y,z)=k$ at the point $({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n∇f({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})\\cdot ⟨x-{x}_{0},\\,y-{y}_{0},\\,z-{z}_{0}⟩=0.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the gradient of $f(x,y,z)$ and evaluate it at $({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})=(1,1,-1):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\,f(x,y,z) & ={f}_{x}(x,y,z)\\,i+{f}_{y}(x,y,z)\\,j+{f}_{z}(x,y,z)\\,k \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}z+{z}^{2}y+{y}^{2}x)\\text{ }i+\\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{2}z+{z}^{2}y+{y}^{2}x)\\text{ }j+\\frac{∂}{∂z}({x}^{2}z+{z}^{2}y+{y}^{2}x)\\text{ }k \\\\  & =(2xz+{y}^{2})\\text{ }i+({z}^{2}+2yx)\\text{ }j+({x}^{2}+2zy)k \\\\ ∇\\,f(1,1,-1) & =(2(1)(-1)+{1}^{2})\\text{ }i+((-1)^{2}+2(1)(1))\\text{ }j+({1}^{2}+2(-1)(1))k \\\\  & =-\\,i+3\\,j-k \\\\  & =⟨-1,3,-1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now write down the Cartesian equation of the tangent plane to the level surface, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})\\cdot ⟨x-{x}_{0},\\,y-{y}_{0},\\,z-{z}_{0}⟩ & =0 \\\\ ∇f(1,1,-1)\\cdot ⟨x-1,\\,y-1,\\,z+1⟩ & =0 \\\\ ⟨-1,3,-1⟩\\cdot ⟨x-1,\\,y-1,\\,z+1⟩ & =0 \\\\ -(x-1)+3(y-1)-(z+1) & =0 \\\\ -x+3y-z-3 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186475921 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129079 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "da47f01b-0db0-586f-9d55-5bd4c952afb6" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Tangent to Plane a Level Surface"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "440544e1-5f06-52ff-99db-005b9668278c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨3,2,1⟩\\cdot ⟨x-2,\\,y+1,\\,z-1⟩=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475545} {:answer/id #uuid "49829757-9104-555e-bbc2-466f13d511b8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨1,-2,-5⟩\\cdot ⟨x+2,\\,y+1,\\,z+1⟩=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475554} {:answer/id #uuid "590b7282-8f58-56dc-9916-0e4a8b5f75e1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨1,1,1⟩\\cdot ⟨x+2,\\,y+1,\\,z+1⟩=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475571} {:answer/id #uuid "a253e227-cf9e-5131-b048-012a2756202f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨1,-2,1⟩\\cdot ⟨x-2,\\,y+1,\\,z-1⟩=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475681} {:answer/id #uuid "ba4e5f22-49b8-59c1-8cb5-9d5d8f6e3159" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨2,1,5⟩\\cdot ⟨x-2,\\,y+1,\\,z-1⟩=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475724}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ba4e5f22-49b8-59c1-8cb5-9d5d8f6e3159" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨2,1,5⟩\\cdot ⟨x-2,\\,y+1,\\,z-1⟩=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475724} :answer-field/id #uuid "fcbbc700-14d3-56d7-9524-57ed54783857" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475907}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "213d84af-097e-53bb-ad1d-ed8419f53f21" :question/math-academy-id "q-102708" :question/problem "Given the function $f(x,y,z)={y}^{3}z-xy+x{z}^{3}$, find the equation of the tangent plane to the level surface that passes through the point where $(x,y,z)=(2,-1,1).$" :question/worked-solution "The equation of the tangent plane to the level surface $f(x,y,z)=k$ at the point $({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n∇f({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})\\cdot ⟨x-{x}_{0},\\,y-{y}_{0},\\,z-{z}_{0}⟩=0.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the gradient of $f(x,y,z)$ and evaluate it at $({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})=(2,-1,1):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\,f(x,y,z) & ={f}_{x}(x,y,z)\\,i+{f}_{y}(x,y,z)\\,j+{f}_{z}(x,y,z)\\,k \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({y}^{3}z-xy+x{z}^{3})\\text{ }i+\\frac{∂}{∂y}({y}^{3}z-xy+x{z}^{3})\\text{ }j+\\frac{∂}{∂z}({y}^{3}z-xy+x{z}^{3})\\text{ }k \\\\  & =({z}^{3}-y)\\text{ }i+(3z{y}^{2}-x)\\text{ }j+(3x{z}^{2}+{y}^{3})k \\\\ ∇\\,f(2,-1,1) & =({1}^{3}-(-1))\\text{ }i+(3(1)(-1)^{2}-2)\\text{ }j+(3(2)(1)^{2}+(-1)^{3})k \\\\  & =2\\,i+\\,j+5k \\\\  & =⟨2,1,5⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now write down the Cartesian equation of the tangent plane to the level surface, as follows: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})\\cdot ⟨x-{x}_{0},\\,y-{y}_{0},\\,z-{z}_{0}⟩ & =0 \\\\ ∇f(2,-1,1)\\cdot ⟨x-2,\\,y+1,\\,z-1⟩ & =0 \\\\ ⟨2,1,5⟩\\cdot ⟨x-2,\\,y+1,\\,z-1⟩ & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186475934 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129179 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "16f4bd05-1f30-576c-a538-a0ac4d533b7a" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Tangent Plane of a Surface Given Implicitly Using the Gradient Vector"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "06ddc08d-d22f-5193-bf06-38fb8c7ba7c7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475455} {:answer/id #uuid "0af3f2c2-59c9-5249-a2d8-811877a6ca18" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475461} {:answer/id #uuid "19987fb0-bc40-51ba-b84d-d8cb0087f00a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{\\pi }" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475476} {:answer/id #uuid "226d0641-c568-50b8-93be-58d7db8760ad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475487} {:answer/id #uuid "87b7e1f6-b074-5206-8b9b-5827ab7b73bd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{{\\pi }^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475648}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0af3f2c2-59c9-5249-a2d8-811877a6ca18" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475461} :answer-field/id #uuid "32ad6879-6146-512a-b9ce-7b997929ffe5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475843}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "480ef21f-535f-5e73-9903-6cc50742dda8" :question/math-academy-id "q-102713" :question/problem "Consider the surface $z\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x+y)-xyz=2+\\frac{{\\pi }^{2}}{2}.$ Given that $n=⟨a,b,c⟩$ is a non-zero normal vector to the surface at the point $(\\frac{\\pi }{2},-\\frac{\\pi }{2},2),$ what is the value of $\\frac{a}{b}?$" :question/worked-solution "Let's define  $f(x,y,z)=z\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x+y)-xyz.$ Then, our surface can be viewed as the level surface $f(x,y,z)=2+\\frac{{\\pi }^{2}}{2}.$  \n\nNow, we find the gradient of $f(x,y,z)$ and evaluate it at $(\\frac{\\pi }{2},-\\frac{\\pi }{2},2):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y,z) & ={f}_{x}(x,y,z)\\,i+{f}_{y}(x,y,z)\\,j+{f}_{z}(x,y,z)\\,k \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(z\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x+y)-xyz)i+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(z\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x+y)-xyz)j+\\frac{∂}{∂z}(z\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x+y)-xyz)k \\\\  & =(-z\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+y)-yz)i+(-z\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+y)-xz)j+(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x+y)-xy)k \\\\ ∇f(\\frac{\\pi }{2},-\\frac{\\pi }{2},2) & =(-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2}-\\frac{\\pi }{2})-2(-\\frac{\\pi }{2}))\\text{ }i+(-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2}-\\frac{\\pi }{2})-2(\\frac{\\pi }{2}))\\text{ }j+(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2}-\\frac{\\pi }{2})-(\\frac{\\pi }{2})(-\\frac{\\pi }{2}))\\text{ }k \\\\  & =\\pi \\text{ }i-\\pi \\text{ }j+(1+\\frac{{\\pi }^{2}}{4})\\text{ }k \\\\  & =⟨\\pi ,\\,-\\pi ,\\,1+\\frac{{\\pi }^{2}}{4}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our normal vector is $n=⟨a,b,c⟩=⟨\\pi ,\\,-\\pi ,\\,\\frac{{\\pi }^{2}+4}{4}⟩.$\n\nFinally, $\\frac{a}{b}=\\frac{\\pi }{-\\pi }=-1.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186475928 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129179 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "16f4bd05-1f30-576c-a538-a0ac4d533b7a" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Tangent Plane of a Surface Given Implicitly Using the Gradient Vector"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "64714f8f-6e99-5b47-ad35-de287d9165d4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x+2y-4z+15=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475591} {:answer/id #uuid "7117415a-5ef5-5b3e-832a-e0fb18a5246f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5x-3y+2z-11=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475601} {:answer/id #uuid "8b61f94e-dc56-526e-824a-66c203febdf4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3x+4y+z-10=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475653} {:answer/id #uuid "9c45389e-541e-5ac3-aa83-a1435e6c3bd8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5x+4y-4z+18=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475673} {:answer/id #uuid "e3a78e06-677c-5f95-89c0-1f507b59be9d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x-y-3z+11=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475792}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9c45389e-541e-5ac3-aa83-a1435e6c3bd8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5x+4y-4z+18=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475673} :answer-field/id #uuid "f5f7cc0c-f2cb-5ebd-8a19-e3ddc8cdda4a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475905}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2dcb9c2a-7362-5965-b423-4b434eec8d3a" :question/math-academy-id "q-102714" :question/problem "Consider the surface $x{y}^{2}+6=z{x}^{2}.$ Find the equation of the tangent plane to that surface at the point $(-2,-1,1).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we bring all variables to one side:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x{y}^{2}+6 & =z{x}^{2} \\\\ x{y}^{2}-z{x}^{2} & =-6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we set $f(x,y,z)=x{y}^{2}-z{x}^{2}$, our surface can be viewed as the level surface $f(x,y,z)=-6.$ \n\nRecall that the equation of the tangent plane to the level surface $f(x,y,z)=k$ at the point $({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n∇f({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})\\cdot ⟨x-{x}_{0},\\,y-{y}_{0},\\,z-{z}_{0}⟩=0.\n$$\n\nNow, we find the gradient of $f(x,y,z)$ and evaluate it at $(-2,-1,1):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\,f(x,y,z) & ={f}_{x}(x,y,z)\\,i+{f}_{y}(x,y,z)\\,j+{f}_{z}(x,y,z)\\,k \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(x{y}^{2}-z{x}^{2})\\text{ }i+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(x{y}^{2}-z{x}^{2})\\text{ }j+\\frac{∂}{∂z}(x{y}^{2}-z{x}^{2})\\text{ }k \\\\  & =({y}^{2}-2xz)\\text{ }i+2xy\\text{ }j-{x}^{2}\\text{ }k \\\\ ∇\\,f(-2,-1,1) & =((-1)^{2}-2(-2)(1))\\text{ }i+2(-2)(-1)\\text{ }j-(-2)^{2}\\text{ }k \\\\  & =5\\,i+4j-4\\,k \\\\  & =⟨5,4,-4⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can now write down the Cartesian equation of the tangent plane to the level surface, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})\\cdot ⟨x-{x}_{0},\\,y-{y}_{0},\\,z-{z}_{0}⟩ & =0 \\\\ ∇f(-2,-1,1)\\cdot ⟨x+2,\\,y+1,\\,z-1⟩ & =0 \\\\ ⟨5,4,-4⟩\\cdot ⟨x+2,\\,y+1,\\,z-1⟩ & =0 \\\\ 5(x+2)+4(y+1)-4(z-1) & =0 \\\\ 5x+4y-4z+18 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186368502 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129179 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "16f4bd05-1f30-576c-a538-a0ac4d533b7a" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Tangent Plane of a Surface Given Implicitly Using the Gradient Vector"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f31566f3-5a9f-50b0-8133-875da6050b2d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x+y+4z+3=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368504} {:answer/id #uuid "0a4508b7-d6bf-54c2-9c11-8ec5041ce685" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4z-x-y-5=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368505} {:answer/id #uuid "30c0d468-01b5-599b-87fa-e43055e8e8d1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x+y+4z-3=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368506} {:answer/id #uuid "c0d82b5d-43cc-5e7b-be7a-81f6c28fddb6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4x+4y+z-3=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368507} {:answer/id #uuid "37714307-6eae-52a9-ace4-a33d77834680" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4x+4y+z+3=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368508}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "30c0d468-01b5-599b-87fa-e43055e8e8d1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x+y+4z-3=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368506} :answer-field/id #uuid "4631e236-0c05-57c6-a8a7-da1ff59269c1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368503}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2fd20ce6-a0d3-5928-9428-ede66532d00e" :question/math-academy-id "q-37594" :question/problem "Consider the surface $\\operatorname{sin}⁡(y+2{z}^{2})=1-x.$ Find the equation of the tangent plane to that surface at the point $(1,-2,1).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we bring all variables to one side:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(y+2{z}^{2}) & =1-x \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(y+2{z}^{2})+x-1 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nIf we set $f(x,y,z)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(y+2{z}^{2})+x-1$, our surface can be viewed as the level surface $f(x,y,z)=0.$\n\nRecall that the equation of the tangent plane to the level surface $f(x,y,z)=k$ at the point $({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n∇f({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})\\cdot ⟨x-{x}_{0},\\,y-{y}_{0},\\,z-{z}_{0}⟩=0.\n$$\n\nNow, we find the gradient of $f(x,y,z)$ and evaluate it at $(1,-2,1):$  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\,f(x,y,z) & ={f}_{x}(x,y,z)\\,i+{f}_{y}(x,y,z)\\,j+{f}_{z}(x,y,z)\\,k \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡(y+2{z}^{2})+x-1\\,)\\text{ }i+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡(y+2{z}^{2})+x-1\\,)\\text{ }j+\\frac{∂}{∂z}(\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡(y+2{z}^{2})+x-1\\,)\\text{ }k \\\\  & =\\text{ }i+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(y+2{z}^{2})\\text{ }j+4z\\operatorname{cos}⁡(y+2{z}^{2})\\text{ }k \\\\ ∇\\,f(1,-2,1) & =\\text{ }i+\\operatorname{cos}⁡((-2)+2(1)^{2})\\text{ }j+4(1)\\operatorname{cos}⁡((-2)+2(1)^{2})\\text{ }k \\\\  & =i+j+4\\,k \\\\  & =⟨1,1,4⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can now write down the Cartesian equation of the tangent plane to the level surface, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})\\cdot ⟨x-{x}_{0},\\,y-{y}_{0},\\,z-{z}_{0}⟩ & =0 \\\\ ∇f(1,-2,1)\\cdot ⟨x-1,\\,y+2,\\,z-1⟩ & =0 \\\\ ⟨1,1,4⟩\\cdot ⟨x-1,\\,y+2,\\,z-1⟩ & =0 \\\\ (x-1)+(y+2)+4(z-1) & =0 \\\\ x+y+4z-3 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186475970 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129079 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "da47f01b-0db0-586f-9d55-5bd4c952afb6" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Tangent to Plane a Level Surface"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "118cc1f0-9337-59db-a9ad-2a4ae699fd03" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-3,2,-1⟩\\cdot ⟨x-2,\\,y-2,\\,z+1⟩=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475469} {:answer/id #uuid "2b8565b0-e89e-5f6d-adc3-e3eee5e42dbe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨1,1,-2⟩\\cdot ⟨x+3,\\,y-2,\\,z+1⟩=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475501} {:answer/id #uuid "6b54833d-6efe-5aa7-b052-fc09a0cc3fc2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨1,1,-2⟩\\cdot ⟨x-1,\\,y-1,\\,z+3⟩=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475599} {:answer/id #uuid "b58b31d8-759f-5627-8ed4-936313cafdc4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨1,1,2⟩\\cdot ⟨x-1,\\,y-1,\\,z-2⟩=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475715} {:answer/id #uuid "e0af46fb-73d6-5868-8ffd-382ee5e4c385" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-3,2,-1⟩\\cdot ⟨x-1,\\,y-1,\\,z-2⟩=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475785}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e0af46fb-73d6-5868-8ffd-382ee5e4c385" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-3,2,-1⟩\\cdot ⟨x-1,\\,y-1,\\,z-2⟩=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475785} :answer-field/id #uuid "b758f2b0-ee02-5c9d-8c7b-99e5dc8caa68" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475882}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d960c3a0-bbd5-5487-b90e-ade524992bee" :question/math-academy-id "q-80763" :question/problem "Given the function $f(x,y,z)=x+{y}^{2}-{x}^{2}z$, find the equation of the tangent plane to the level surface that passes through the point where $(x,y,z)=(1,1,2).$" :question/worked-solution "The equation of the tangent plane to the level surface $f(x,y,z)=k$ at the point $({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n∇f({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})\\cdot ⟨x-{x}_{0},\\,y-{y}_{0},\\,z-{z}_{0}⟩=0.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the gradient of $f(x,y,z)$ and evaluate it at $({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})=(1,1,2):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\,f(x,y,z) & ={f}_{x}(x,y,z)\\,i+{f}_{y}(x,y,z)\\,j+{f}_{z}(x,y,z)\\,k \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(x+{y}^{2}-{x}^{2}z)\\text{ }i+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(x+{y}^{2}-{x}^{2}z)\\text{ }j+\\frac{∂}{∂z}(x+{y}^{2}-{x}^{2}z)\\text{ }k \\\\  & =(1-2xz)\\text{ }i+2y\\text{ }j-{x}^{2}k \\\\ ∇\\,f(1,1,2) & =(\\,1-2(1)(2)\\,)\\text{ }i+2(1)\\text{ }j-(1)^{2}k \\\\  & =-3\\,i+2\\,j-1\\,k \\\\  & =⟨-3,2,-1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now write down the Cartesian equation of the tangent plane to the level surface, as follows: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})\\cdot ⟨x-{x}_{0},\\,y-{y}_{0},\\,z-{z}_{0}⟩ & =0 \\\\ ∇f(1,1,2)\\cdot ⟨x-1,\\,y-1,\\,z-2⟩ & =0 \\\\ ⟨-3,2,-1⟩\\cdot ⟨x-1,\\,y-1,\\,z-2⟩ & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186348448 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129079 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "da47f01b-0db0-586f-9d55-5bd4c952afb6" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Tangent to Plane a Level Surface"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1663e019-c7d9-5e2d-9dbe-71ebddf8290b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x+2y+7z-36=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186345549} {:answer/id #uuid "6571ddc7-83ee-51ae-b69b-3a73f8b9bf0a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8x+y+z-23=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346236} {:answer/id #uuid "925d13bb-c92d-5f35-b0f3-4234c87d30e9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8x+2y+5z+7=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346631} {:answer/id #uuid "c6840705-8e54-503e-be26-3574f6f8d412" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x+y+z-9=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347078} {:answer/id #uuid "e082281f-2341-5fb5-83fb-0ba87ed7944d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x+2y+5z-28=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347320}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e082281f-2341-5fb5-83fb-0ba87ed7944d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x+2y+5z-28=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347320} :answer-field/id #uuid "c9a7661b-5846-57e9-be3c-6d40db58cd30" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347954}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "bbcded61-18ec-5362-9f48-c67e58a60e0a" :question/math-academy-id "q-80767" :question/problem "Given the function $f(x,y,z)=xy-yz-xz$, find the equation of the tangent plane to the level surface that passes  through the point where $(x,y,z)=(2,3,4).$" :question/worked-solution "The equation of the tangent plane to the level surface $f(x,y,z)=k$ at the point $({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n∇f({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})\\cdot ⟨x-{x}_{0},\\,y-{y}_{0},\\,z-{z}_{0}⟩=0.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the gradient of $f(x,y,z)$ and evaluate it at $({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})=(2,3,4):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\,f(x,y,z) & ={f}_{x}(x,y,z)\\,i+{f}_{y}(x,y,z)\\,j+{f}_{z}(x,y,z)\\,k \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(xy-yz-xz)\\text{ }i+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(xy-yz-xz)\\text{ }j+\\frac{∂}{∂z}(xy-yz-xz)\\text{ }k \\\\  & =(y-z)\\text{ }i+(x-z)\\text{ }j+(-y-x)k \\\\ ∇\\,f(2,3,4) & =(3-4)\\text{ }i+(2-4)\\text{ }j+(-3-2)k \\\\  & =-1\\text{ }i-2\\text{ }j-5k \\\\  & =⟨-1,-2,-5⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nWe can now write down the Cartesian equation of the tangent plane to the level surface, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})\\cdot ⟨x-{x}_{0},\\,y-{y}_{0},\\,z-{z}_{0}⟩ & =0 \\\\ ∇f(2,3,4)\\cdot ⟨x-2,\\,y-3,\\,z-4⟩ & =0 \\\\ ⟨-1,-2,-5⟩\\cdot ⟨x-2,\\,y-3,\\,z-4⟩ & =0 \\\\ -(x-2)-2(y-3)-5(z-4) & =0 \\\\ -x-2y-5z+28 & =0 \\\\ x+2y+5z-28 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186348449 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129079 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "da47f01b-0db0-586f-9d55-5bd4c952afb6" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Tangent to Plane a Level Surface"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "34d6c237-b645-5134-bed0-3db87cd111a1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x+8y+4z-14=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186345809} {:answer/id #uuid "5451ea98-cec6-5c7d-adef-f96ea6bd234c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x+4y+4z-10=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346066} {:answer/id #uuid "8e60e7e0-b0eb-5453-8a9e-93ecd04c25ae" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x+8y+z-13=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346590} {:answer/id #uuid "cfc13077-10ec-5459-801a-f68bf9ba6620" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x+2y+z-5=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347169} {:answer/id #uuid "f41a2ef9-7eb7-5e8a-8edf-fd77bb60489a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x+y+z-6=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347514}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cfc13077-10ec-5459-801a-f68bf9ba6620" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x+2y+z-5=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347169} :answer-field/id #uuid "384d5f4d-e2ac-598f-9b2f-eabbb7bb39e6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347700}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "4798bf87-b861-5528-ad8e-12b959ab1ff8" :question/math-academy-id "q-80769" :question/problem "Given the function $f(x,y,z)={x}^{2}+4{y}^{2}+2{z}^{2}$,  find the equation of the tangent plane to the level surface that passes through the point where $(x,y,z)=(2,1,1).$" :question/worked-solution "The equation of the tangent plane to the level surface $f(x,y,z)=k$ at the point $({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n∇\\,f({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})\\cdot ⟨x-{x}_{0},\\,y-{y}_{0},\\,z-{z}_{0}⟩=0.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the gradient of $f(x,y,z)$ and evaluate it at $({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})=(2,1,1):$  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\,f(x,y,z) & ={f}_{x}(x,y,z)\\,i+{f}_{y}(x,y,z)\\,j+{f}_{z}(x,y,z)\\,k \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}+4{y}^{2}+2{z}^{2})\\text{ }i+\\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{2}+4{y}^{2}+2{z}^{2})\\text{ }j+\\frac{∂}{∂z}({x}^{2}+4{y}^{2}+2{z}^{2})\\text{ }k \\\\  & =2x\\text{ }i+8y\\text{ }j+4z\\text{ }k \\\\ ∇\\,f(2,1,1) & =2(2)\\text{ }i+8(1)j+4(1)\\text{ }k \\\\  & =4\\,i+8\\,j+4\\,k \\\\  & =⟨4,8,4⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nWe can now write down the Cartesian equation of the tangent plane to the level surface, as follows: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\,f({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})\\cdot ⟨x-{x}_{0},\\,y-{y}_{0},\\,z-{z}_{0}⟩ & =0 \\\\ ∇\\,f(2,1,1)\\cdot ⟨x-2,\\,y-1,\\,z-1⟩ & =0 \\\\ ⟨4,8,4⟩\\cdot ⟨x-2,\\,y-1,\\,z-1⟩ & =0 \\\\ 4(x-2)+8(y-1)+4(z-1) & =0 \\\\ 4x+8y+4z-20 & =0 \\\\ x+2y+z-5 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186475932 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129179 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "16f4bd05-1f30-576c-a538-a0ac4d533b7a" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Tangent Plane of a Surface Given Implicitly Using the Gradient Vector"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3fd0afb4-7f63-53a1-b9d8-fc43a52190f4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475536} {:answer/id #uuid "5ad2b351-e9e7-5fc0-88f8-4819b6585606" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "17" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475573} {:answer/id #uuid "b516ade3-ffe4-53e7-a108-f173e4ed48c0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475714} {:answer/id #uuid "dd536e1c-8382-55ff-9267-96684e811590" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475779} {:answer/id #uuid "e7b47223-ff42-5c40-a1d5-3c7146f22c5e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475797}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e7b47223-ff42-5c40-a1d5-3c7146f22c5e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475797} :answer-field/id #uuid "090b5739-81c2-5833-b9c4-518b63612c50" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475833}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "417fb447-d242-53ba-be44-8afd73288884" :question/math-academy-id "q-80781" :question/problem "Consider the surface ${x}^{2}{y}^{2}+{e}^{z-1}=17.$ Given that $n=⟨a,b,c⟩$ is a non-zero normal vector to the surface at the point $(2,-2,1),$ what is the value of $\\frac{a}{c}?$" :question/worked-solution "Let's define  $f(x,y,z)={x}^{2}{y}^{2}+{e}^{z-1}.$ Then, our surface can be viewed as the level surface $f(x,y,z)=17.$   \n\nNow, we find the gradient of $f(x,y,z)$ and evaluate it at $(2,-2,1):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y,z) & ={f}_{x}(x,y,z)\\,i+{f}_{y}(x,y,z)\\,j+{f}_{z}(x,y,z)\\,k \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}{y}^{2}+{e}^{z-1}))i+\\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{2}{y}^{2}+{e}^{z-1})j+\\frac{∂}{∂z}({x}^{2}{y}^{2}+{e}^{z-1}))k \\\\  & =2x{y}^{2}i+2y{x}^{2}j+{e}^{z-1}k \\\\ ∇f(2,-2,1) & =2(2)(-2)^{2}\\text{ }i+2(-2){2}^{2}\\text{ }j+{e}^{1-1}\\text{ }k \\\\  & =16\\text{ }i-16\\text{ }j+\\text{ }k \\\\  & =⟨16,\\,-16,\\,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our normal vector is $n=⟨a,b,c⟩=⟨16,\\,-16,\\,1⟩.$ \n\nFinally, $\\frac{a}{c}=\\frac{16}{1}=16.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186368852 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129179 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "16f4bd05-1f30-576c-a538-a0ac4d533b7a" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Tangent Plane of a Surface Given Implicitly Using the Gradient Vector"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "14878a31-11ea-5c7e-84d0-fd09663b9dec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "11x-24y+z+62=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368854} {:answer/id #uuid "93faa97f-405e-5443-9dbd-03d61733af8c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "11x-4y-z+62=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368855} {:answer/id #uuid "b05712f5-94c2-5c99-92eb-789baeed8e32" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x-24y+z+26=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368856} {:answer/id #uuid "17bfc5b8-7e32-54b3-ac77-8535f2ab4942" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x-42y+11z-26=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368857} {:answer/id #uuid "a8436930-5933-58e8-ba5e-4ae3f1d425c8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "11x+24y+z-62=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368858}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "14878a31-11ea-5c7e-84d0-fd09663b9dec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "11x-24y+z+62=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368854} :answer-field/id #uuid "a4bef21b-f7ad-5f9a-819c-86eb77bec1f5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368853}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "57e1cfb5-fa24-5598-9daa-442855c8439f" :question/math-academy-id "q-86470" :question/problem "Consider the surface $z{x}^{4}+18=x+2{y}^{3}.$ Find the equation of the tangent plane to that surface at the point $(-1,2,-3).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we bring all variables to one side:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z{x}^{4}+18 & =x+2{y}^{3} \\\\ z{x}^{4}-x-2{y}^{3} & =-18\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we set $f(x,y,z)=z{x}^{4}-x-2{y}^{3},$ our surface can be viewed as the level surface $f(x,y,z)=-18.$ \n\nRecall that the equation of the tangent plane to the level surface $f(x,y,z)=k$ at the point $({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n∇f({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})\\cdot ⟨x-{x}_{0},\\,y-{y}_{0},\\,z-{z}_{0}⟩=0.\n$$\n\nNow, we find the gradient of $f(x,y,z)$ and evaluate it at $(-1,2,-3):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\,f(x,y,z) & ={f}_{x}(x,y,z)\\,i+{f}_{y}(x,y,z)\\,j+{f}_{z}(x,y,z)\\,k \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(z{x}^{4}-x-2{y}^{3})\\text{ }i+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(z{x}^{4}-x-2{y}^{3})\\text{ }j+\\frac{∂}{∂z}(z{x}^{4}-x-2{y}^{3})\\text{ }k \\\\  & =(4{x}^{3}z-1)\\text{ }i-6{y}^{2}\\text{ }j+{x}^{4}\\text{ }k \\\\ ∇\\,f(-1,2,-3) & =(4(-1)^{3}(-3)-1)\\text{ }i-6(2)^{2}\\text{ }j+(-1)^{4}\\text{ }k \\\\  & =11\\,i-24j+k \\\\  & =⟨11,-24,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can now write down the Cartesian equation of the tangent plane to the level surface, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})\\cdot ⟨x-{x}_{0},\\,y-{y}_{0},\\,z-{z}_{0}⟩ & =0 \\\\ ∇f(-1,2,-3)\\cdot ⟨x+1,\\,y-2,\\,z+3⟩ & =0 \\\\ ⟨11,-24,1⟩\\cdot ⟨x+1,\\,y-2,\\,z+3⟩ & =0 \\\\ 11(x+1)-24(y-2)+(z+3) & =0 \\\\ 11x-24y+z+62 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
